      "content": "exactly. i was looking closer at the timestamped intervals. between 03:12 and 03:18 UTC, the deviations seemed to follow a sort of 3-1-4-1 pattern in the pitch oscillation. it's too consistent to be random jitter. if you look at the way the NOAA sat responded right after the Starlink cluster shifted, it almost looked like a handshake. do you see any way these specific sequences could be interpreted as a data transmission or a protocol trigger?",
